{"title":"2022 SSMO Relay Round 2 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_2_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a randomly selected point on a circle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a randomly selected point inside the same circle. A dilation centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with a scale factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sends <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/6/1764a2c9321cb2437b9074adfcdab44fa3199807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA&#39;$\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is less than the length of the diameter of the circle can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9accd14040f626162a32cf09e85ca926ae3ab09f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\pi+b\\sqrt{c}}{d\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a squarefree positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a643bcc8195884f4fc1e16966f6f3d6ad6fe2c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e947add5766b9f26f6dfe73d9425d87664416459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_2_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7107258060287e39c3461af1bee0dd7cc3c945.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(6cm); pair X = (1/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair P = (1,0); pair O = (0,0);  filldraw(arc(O,1,-60,60)--O--cycle,lightgray,invisible); filldraw(arc(P,1,120,240)--P--cycle,lightgray,invisible); draw(circle(O,1)); draw(arc(P,1,100,260),blue+dashed); draw(P--O--X--cycle,magenta+dashed);  dot(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,E); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,W); dot(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,N); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"265\" /> </center><p> Assume WLOG that the circle is a unit circle and fix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Draw a unit circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> to be less than the length of the radius of the circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> must lie in the shaded region. To compute the area of the shaded region, we divide it into two equal halves through line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcc9ecb8e7c6fb80766c186721353e6c3dc398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Then, we can compute the area of each half by adding the areas of arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a903f7c677cbaadb6e72741b95730648ab1d442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fc2c59d25e97ec515446444b44cbe415d3f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> and subtracting the overlapping equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008e1c73552833fd8634d0a689bd6e09100311b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$POX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> of sidelength <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This gives an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb29f43e74fd921bb2b7c167d4a58e3125a8bcbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"53\" /> and a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa96e5435085503cfec0ca364de92cfc97a09352.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{\\pi}=\\frac{4\\pi-3\\sqrt{3}}{6\\pi}\\implies 4+3+3+6=\\boxed{16}.\\]\" width=\"371\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022017\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 96/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4362/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26219:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022017 and revision id 280186. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}